1
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:06,870
On April the eighteenth, 2018, in a store
car park in Roseville, California,

2
00:00:07,300 --> 00:00:10,090
a detective swabbed the door
handle of a parked car.

3
00:00:10,680 --> 00:00:14,260
Five days later, another detective
took a used tissue from a trash

4
00:00:14,280 --> 00:00:15,950
can outside the owner's house.

5
00:00:16,420 --> 00:00:17,670
Both went to a lab.

6
00:00:19,560 --> 00:00:23,710
They matched DNA left at the scene
of a double murder in 1980.

7
00:00:24,660 --> 00:00:27,920
For thirty-eight years, that
DNA had matched no one.

8
00:00:27,940 --> 00:00:31,920
The man it came from had never been
arrested, so he had never been

9
00:00:31,940 --> 00:00:33,450
in any police database.

10
00:00:35,690 --> 00:00:37,640
He wasn't found in a police database.

11
00:00:38,150 --> 00:00:41,930
He was found through his relatives:
cousins who had sent their DNA

12
00:00:41,950 --> 00:00:46,080
to genealogy websites to find out
where their families came from.

13
00:00:48,240 --> 00:00:49,470
None of them was asked.

14
00:00:50,100 --> 00:00:51,750
Most have never been named.

15
00:00:52,300 --> 00:00:56,220
And before the search found the right
man, it pointed at the wrong

16
00:00:56,240 --> 00:00:56,690
one.

17
00:00:59,610 --> 00:01:01,910
The man was the Golden State Killer.

18
00:01:02,460 --> 00:01:07,780
Between the mid-1970s and 1986, he
murdered thirteen people in California

19
00:01:07,800 --> 00:01:09,990
and attacked dozens more.

20
00:01:10,620 --> 00:01:12,750
In 2020 he pleaded guilty.

21
00:01:13,240 --> 00:01:15,130
He is serving life without parole.

22
00:01:17,630 --> 00:01:19,820
His arrest made the method famous.

23
00:01:20,630 --> 00:01:24,560
Since then, police have used it in
well over a thousand cases.

24
00:01:24,890 --> 00:01:28,300
And you don't have to take a DNA
test to be found by it.

25
00:01:28,670 --> 00:01:29,840
A cousin is enough.

26
00:01:31,700 --> 00:01:34,710
So, should police be allowed to
search your family's DNA?

27
00:01:35,540 --> 00:01:39,570
When one person shares their DNA, they
share part of their relatives'

28
00:01:39,660 --> 00:01:43,030
DNA too. Who gets to say
yes for a family?

29
00:01:43,600 --> 00:01:46,310
And what should the state be
allowed to do with the answer?
